  "question": {
    "text": "Two communicating vessels contain mercury. The diameter of one vessel is <math><mi>n</mi></math> times larger than the diameter of the other. A column of water of height <math><mi>h</mi></math> is poured into the left vessel. The mercury level will rise in the right-hand vessel (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi></math> = relative density of mercury and <math><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo></math> density of water) by<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0059_daabc6648fb7.png\" style=\"width: 272px; height: 114px;\" />"
  },
